# Yugo bot — required
YUGO_MODE=
TASK_STATE_PATH=
COORDINATOR_HEARTBEAT_MS=
# The three required keys below carry EXAMPLE-ONLY values so this file can
# double as CI's docker smoke-gate env-file (SPEC §11): `.env.example` is
# what the documented quick-start's `.env` derives from, so any blank or
# unparseable value would restart-loop the container on the operator's
# happy path. Replace ALL three before deploying — the DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN
# sentinel will fail Discord auth loudly if shipped as-is; CHANNEL_ID=1
# matches no real channel so a mis-deploy silently ignores every message.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=REQUIRED_paste_your_discord_bot_token
CHANNEL_ID=1
MODEL=xai/grok-code-fast-1

# Provider API key — set the one your MODEL uses.
# See https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers for model-string → env-var mapping.
XAI_API_KEY=REQUIRED_if_MODEL_starts_with_xai_slash
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Ollama / self-hosted: OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Optional
GUILD_ID=
TIMEZONE=UTC
RESPONSE_TIMEOUT=120
PERSONA_FILE=/root/persona.md
# Rolling per-thread history buffer (v0.2a). A "turn" = user + assistant, so
# the underlying deque holds HISTORY_MAX_TURNS*2 messages. Default: 10.
HISTORY_MAX_TURNS=10
# The same bound for fleet-bus turns (v0.3b), which keep their own per-peer
# history namespace — a bus turn never sees Discord context and vice versa.
# Separate knob on purpose: this one decides how long another bot's untrusted
# content keeps shaping replies. Read only when FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=1 matters;
# harmless otherwise. Default: 10.
BUS_HISTORY_MAX_TURNS=10

# Tool-use grants (v0.4b+). This read-only YAML file is the sole capability
# source; persona prose declares nothing. Absent or empty grants zero tools.
# See SPEC §9.1 for the fail-closed grammar. Default: /etc/yugo/tools.yaml.
YUGO_TOOLS_FILE=/etc/yugo/tools.yaml
YUGO_HTTP_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/etc/yugo/http-credentials.yaml
# Created mode 0700 only when a filesystem tool is granted. Blank selects
# /var/lib/yugo/workspace/<BOT_NAME>.
YUGO_WORKSPACE_PATH=
#
# TOOL_MAX_ROUNDS bounds how many times one turn may go model → tools → model
# before it gives up. RESPONSE_TIMEOUT still bounds the turn as a WHOLE, so
# raising this cannot make a turn outlive it. Default: 5.
TOOL_MAX_ROUNDS=5
# Per-call audit trail: args, result summary, duration (SPEC §9). Keep it
# OUTSIDE whatever workspace v0.4b's `write_file` gets scoped to, or the bot
# can rewrite its own audit. Default: /var/lib/yugo/tool-audit.jsonl.
YUGO_TOOL_AUDIT_PATH=/var/lib/yugo/tool-audit.jsonl

# Tool sandbox mode (v0.4e). `reduced` is the default and the only implemented
# mode: SPEC §9's cheap-important guards are on (http_get default-deny with
# address pinning, workspace-confined file tools, tamper-proof audit path, no
# docker socket) and the expensive ones are deferred.
#
# Setting `full` is a STARTUP ABORT, not a silent downgrade. You set it when
# the threat model changed, and running reduced under a full label would be a
# lie you had no way to notice. Unknown values abort for the same reason.
# Left commented out so this file stays usable as CI's smoke-gate env-file.
# SANDBOX_MODE=reduced

# fleet-bus adapter (v0.3a — connect + subscribe + heartbeat + audit).
# With FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=0 none of the keys below are read and nats-py is
# never imported. With FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=1, BOT_NAME + FLEET_BUS_TOKEN_FILE +
# a readable manifest are ALL required and the bot refuses to start without
# them (same fatal class as a missing persona). A NATS server that is simply
# unreachable is not fatal — the bot serves Discord and retries forever.
FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=0
# Canonical fleet identity: ^[a-z0-9_-]+$, must appear in the manifest's
# bot_names, and must equal FLEET_BUS_USER. Builds every `fleet.<self>.*`
# subject. Required only when FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=1.
#
# It also names the container in compose.yml (`container_name: ${BOT_NAME:-yugo}`),
# which IS read with the bus off — set it per bot or two bots on one host fight
# over the name `yugo`. Left blank here so this file stays usable as CI's
# smoke-gate env-file; blank falls back to `yugo`.
BOT_NAME=
FLEET_BUS_URL=nats://nats:4222
# Defaults to BOT_NAME. Set it only to make the pairing explicit — a value
# that differs from BOT_NAME is a startup abort, not a silent override.
FLEET_BUS_USER=
FLEET_BUS_TOKEN_FILE=
FLEET_BUS_MANIFEST_PATH=/vault/infra/fleet-manifest.yaml
FLEET_BUS_AUDIT_LOG=/root/.claude/fleet-bus-log.jsonl
# Blank uses /var/lib/yugo/<BOT_NAME>-dedup.sqlite (8-day retention).
YUGO_DEDUP_STORE_PATH=
# Operator-provisioned storage attestation for that store (SPEC-26 §8).
# REQUIRED whenever FLEET_BUS_ENABLED=1 and the store above is a file: a
# file-backed store with no record refuses to open, and the bot refuses to
# start with `dedup verification refused: missing verification record`. The
# value is a path to a JSON record — canonical path, inode, device binding,
# schema fingerprint — that an OPERATOR writes once, out of band. A consumer
# never creates, refreshes or repairs one; self-attestation is not attestation.
#
# Provision it INSIDE the mount the bot actually runs with, or the record binds
# an inode this container never opens and you hit the same refusal having done
# everything right. compose.example.yml mounts `./adapter-state` at
# /var/lib/yugo, so bind that same host directory and name CONTAINER paths:
#   docker run --rm -it -v "$PWD/adapter-state:/var/lib/yugo" \
#     --entrypoint yugo <image> dedup provision --port python \
#     --attested-by "$USER" \
#     --store /var/lib/yugo/<BOT_NAME>-dedup.sqlite \
#     --record /var/lib/yugo/<BOT_NAME>-dedup.record.json
# (entrypoint.sh dispatches bot/coordinator only, hence --entrypoint.) The
# command is interactive on purpose: it makes you confirm every accessor is
# stopped, then paste the storage evidence and accessor inventory you
# inspected. Set this variable to the CONTAINER path it wrote:
#   YUGO_DEDUP_VERIFICATION_RECORD=/var/lib/yugo/<BOT_NAME>-dedup.record.json
#
# RE-ATTESTING an existing store is a DIFFERENT operation — add `--record-only`
# and the command attests the store already there instead of creating one.
# Everything else about the invocation is the same. SPEC-26 §8.5 makes it
# mandatory after a restore from backup or a recreated store, a reboot on a
# `devno` binding, a move to another filesystem, and after ANY change to the
# accessor set: the inventory is part of the evidence, so adding or removing an
# accessor makes the record stale even though nothing moved.
#
# An existing SIX-column store from Release 1 is the §8.6 case, not this one.
# Follow that ordered sequence — stop every accessor, back up WAL-aware,
# `yugo dedup migrate --store ... --backup ... --port python`, then re-attest
# with `--record-only`. A fresh provision is not a substitute and refuses.
#
# Left blank here so this file stays usable as CI's smoke-gate env-file; blank
# is the same refusal as unset.
YUGO_DEDUP_VERIFICATION_RECORD=
